          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "It means a polymer, usually latex or acrylic, has been blended into the asphalt emulsion. The polymer makes the cured film more flexible and more resistant to scuffing, cracking and wear. Most mid- and top-tier retail sealers include some polymer, and contractors often add it in the tank. It is one of the main differences between budget and premium products."
          }
