          Strip away the marketing and every asphalt sealer comes down to a few ingredients: a binder, a carrier, something to keep them mixed, and optional extras like filler, sand and polymer. The ratio of those ingredients, not the brand or the number of years on the front, decides how a sealer covers, how long it lasts and how it behaves in bad weather. This guide explains the chemistry, how retail pails differ from what contractors spray, and which products sit where on that spectrum.
        </p>

        <QuickPicks products={PRODUCTS} />


        <!-- Picks -->
