        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The best asphalt sealer for most homes is a filled, polymer-modified asphalt emulsion. It matches the pavement's own binder, cures with water evaporation, cleans up with a hose and gains real durability from its filler and polymer. Latex-ite Airport Grade is the clearest example, with Black Jack Drive-Maxx 1000 as the premium alternative and Jetcoat Premium for rougher surfaces.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Skip coal tar, treat oil-based products as a niche, and read the data sheet rather than the years on the front of the pail. If you hire a contractor, ask what is in their tank. Chemistry decides how a sealer performs, but prep, weather and two thin coats decide whether that chemistry gets a chance to work.
          </p>
        </div>

